{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-generated-31acc1481df1ab2f","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"common_knowledge","text":"An application fan is the number or pattern of application components that depend directly on, call, or use a particular component, service, or interface. A high application fan indicates broad reuse and means that changes to the shared component may affect many parts of the application.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]}]}
